    "originalByteLength": 28737,
    "sanitizedHtml": "<article class=\"docx-projection\"><p><strong>Margolis DFU Prognostic CKS</strong><strong> Summary</strong></p><p><strong>Purpose. </strong>This CKS estimates the model-based probability that one diabetic foot ulcer will heal by 16 weeks, using only wound area and wound duration measured at the first clinical visit. It is a categorical pretreatment prognosis—not a continuous individualized risk equation, treatment-effect estimate, HBOT eligibility decision, or treatment recommendation.</p><p><strong>2 FIRST-VISIT QUANTITIES  →  EXACT UNIT VALIDATION  →  4-STATE LOOKUP  →  16-WEEK PROGNOSIS</strong></p><h1>What the function receives</h1><p><strong>1. Wound area. </strong>First-visit longest × widest area as a closed Quantity containing only value and UCUM code. Accepted codes are cm2 and mm2; normalized area must be greater than zero.</p><p><strong>2. Wound duration. </strong>Elapsed duration at the same first visit as a closed Quantity containing only value and UCUM code. Accepted codes are wk and d; the supplied value must be nonnegative.</p><p><strong>3. Host boundary. </strong>The host binds both measurements to the same identified ulcer and visit and retains identifiers, dates, measurement provenance, and supporting evidence outside the core payload. The core accepts no additional predictors, dates, comparators, uncertainty, or source fields.</p><h1>What is calculated—and how</h1><p><strong>Exact validation and normalization. </strong>The evaluator validates both closed Quantity objects, parses finite numbers as exact base-10 values, and rejects missing, additional, unsupported, or incompatible content without unit inference, repair, or coercion.</p><p><strong>Threshold classification. </strong>Area is compared in its supplied unit with 2 cm2 or 200 mm2; duration is compared with 8 wk or 56 d. Exact comparisons avoid floating-point boundary drift. Because the source did not specify equality, this CKS assigns equality to the less-favorable ≥2 cm² or ≥8-week stratum.</p><p><strong>Four-state lookup. </strong>The two binary categories select exactly one published probability. The evaluator does not interpolate, use distance from a threshold, reconstruct the continuous logistic equation, or create an ordinal point score.</p><h1>Four-state prognostic lookup</h1><p><strong>All valid inputs match exactly one rule: </strong>probabilities are the published model-based healing rates, not the supplement’s observed group rates. Unit-native equivalents use 200 mm2 and 56 d.</p><table><tbody><tr><th><p><strong>Rule</strong></p></th><th><p><strong>Area condition</strong></p></th><th><p><strong>Duration condition</strong></p></th><th><p><strong>Healing by 16 weeks</strong></p></th></tr><tr><td><p><strong>ALG-01</strong></p></td><td><p><strong>≥2 cm²</strong></p></td><td><p><strong>≥8 weeks</strong></p></td><td><p><strong>20.3%</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>ALG-02</strong></p></td><td><p><strong>≥2 cm²</strong></p></td><td><p><strong>&lt;8 weeks</strong></p></td><td><p><strong>30.4%</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>ALG-03</strong></p></td><td><p><strong>&lt;2 cm²</strong></p></td><td><p><strong>≥8 weeks</strong></p></td><td><p><strong>44.8%</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>ALG-04</strong></p></td><td><p><strong>&lt;2 cm²</strong></p></td><td><p><strong>&lt;8 weeks</strong></p></td><td><p><strong>63.1%</strong></p></td></tr></tbody></table><h1>What is returned</h1><p><strong>Fixed-shape prognosis result. </strong>A successful result returns the rule and prognostic group, decimal and display probability, area and duration categories, exact comparison basis, normalized inputs, source reference, and threshold-equality notes when applicable. A validation failure returns ordered errors and no prognosis. The probability is a group-level 16-week estimate—not a guarantee—and does not account for predictors or treatments outside this two-factor model.</p></article>",
